  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one data point (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), so the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality carries useful signal at all. Testing config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly parallels the RNA baseline structure, isolating the image modality's standalone contribution. If image accuracy is substantially higher than 48.5%, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion strategies; if it is comparable or lower, we should prioritize RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) and multiprofile aggregation instead. This single experiment most efficiently partitions the remaining 8-experiment budget between two very different search directions."
}

